Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Gauge-Fixed Raw H/N Benchmark: (a,c) = (5,1)", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"2caba14e-24c4-d34d-a10c-10da613e57b1"],

Cell["\<\
This notebook uses two independent AdaptiveQuasiMonteCarlo integrations per \
state: one complete Hamiltonian-correction numerator H and one norm \
denominator N. It does not impose a shared fixed point set. The global \
rotation is removed by setting the azimuth of hole a to zero, while every \
remaining relative angle spans [0,2 Pi]. The XX expressions retain raw \
G(P+Q), all six Coulomb terms, and the explicit kinetic terms of all four \
particles. No reflection folding, particle-exchange multiplicity, \
minimization, or production-file modification is used. Every integral is \
timed and checkpointed.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"953b8d21-3331-f641-b176-b916490cff34"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Load definitions", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"6d194110-a9c8-4142-b455-95319ca91ac9"],

